{
 "_note": "The DSX error-system corpus (architecture/proposals/error-system.md, ACCEPTED v1) — every runtime (TS kernel errors.ts, Kotlin Errors.kt, Swift Errors.swift) runs these cases through ITS bus + ledger; deterministic, no timers, no network. THE LAW ENCODED HERE: (1) `dsx.error`/`dsx.fail` on the AMBIENT hat (the module handle — a markup action is always ambient) records a DSXError and is REPEATABLE: no settle guard, every emission records. (2) The wire shape is { code, message?, recoverable, data?, scheme, origin } — code is the only required input; message defaults null, recoverable false, origin 'raised' for ambient emissions, 'call' for bus-call failures (which additionally carry `delivered`: false = fire-and-forget, the call site never saw it), and 'uncaught' for a throw that unwinds a markup action to the top with no catch. (3) Every recorded error fans out: the ledger (ring, cap 128, oldest evicted), the `module.error` hook for ambient emissions (`module.callFailed` stays the transport hook for call failures), the page channel `{scheme, event:'error', data:<wire>}` on the module's OWN scheme PLUS the reserved `dsx` scheme mirror, and the reactive keys `global.dsx.lastError` (wire shape) + `global.dsx.errorCount` (monotonic count). (4) HAT ISOLATION: inside a call, `dsx.error` still settles exactly once (first-call-wins, envelope unchanged) — a second terminal settle is swallowed and records nothing new; ambient semantics never leak into the call hat. (5) A hook's own emission mid-fan-out stays log-only (no recursion). (6) The `dsx` scheme is reserved — a module registering it is refused, `dsx.has('dsx')` stays false — yet the KERNEL answers the `dsx.error` verb on the bus (dispatch scheme 'dsx', action 'error' — the page's `dsx.error(...)` in DSXWebView rides exactly this): args { code, message?, recoverable?, data?, scheme? } run the ambient fan-out attributed to the `scheme` arg (default 'page') and resolve null; an unknown action on `dsx` answers unknown_action honestly. (7) UNCAUGHT CAPTURE: an uncaught markup throw reports through the SAME ambient fan-out with origin 'uncaught' — a thrown dict with a string `code` keeps its code/message/recoverable/data; a codeless dict with a string `message` (a JSE `new Error(…)`, the browser-parity throw) keeps the message and rides whole as data; any other dict rides as data with a null message; any other value records code 'uncaught' with the JSE string coercion as message; a throw settled by `catch` records NOTHING. Case ops: register[] fixture modules (actions: resolve:<value> | error:[code,data] | errorTwice:[c1,c2]); steps[] of emit / emitRepeat / jse (markup body; scheme = surface owner, default 'app') / call (mode await|post, optional args{}); expects are SUBSET-matched: ledger[] = exactly the entries appended by this case in order, ledgerCount = absolute retained total (cap case), events[] = page-channel deliveries in order, hooks{} = observed hook payloads, state{} = global reads after the case, stateDelta{} = numeric deltas, callErrors[] = codes the driven calls received (an awaited call that resolves records nothing), jseStore{} = store reads after a jse step, schemeAvailable{} = registry answers.",
