   "_note": "P3 ADOPTION \u2014 the PAGE half of the migration: a page that trades a module's bespoke error broadcast for the canonical channel must be able to read everything the bespoke payload carried. Both deliveries (the module's OWN scheme and the reserved `dsx` mirror) carry the FULL wire \u2014 code, message, recoverable, scheme, origin AND the free-form `data` the module used to flatten into custom keys (the legacy `{ id, errorCode, errorMessage }` shape rides `data` verbatim). `recoverable` is what one global error toast branches on (offer Retry or not), so the mirror carries it, not just the code.",
