   "_note": "TYPED ABSENCE (durability.md P4): the reason IS the code — the frozen absence vocabulary on the ordinary call-failure path is `excluded` (this build dropped the module — the NEW split out of not_loaded, driven by the build-excluded overlay the resolvers already carry) · `unsupported_platform` (never on this platform — pinned in Conformance/api/wire-contract.json, unchanged) · `prerequisites_missing` and `unreachable` (module/link-emitted, spellings frozen here) — all distinct from `not_loaded` (truly unknown) and `unknown_action`. New case op: `excludedOverlay` seeds the case's build-excluded overlay (chain → { reason: 'excluded' } | { reason: 'cascade', from }) — the DespiaExcluded shape, 1:1 with despia.excluded introspection; the call-failure `data` carries that entry verbatim.",
   "name": "call-to-an-excluded-module-answers-excluded",
   "excludedOverlay": { "errfx.gone": { "reason": "excluded" } },
   "steps": [
    { "call": { "scheme": "errfx.gone", "action": "anything", "mode": "await" } }
   ],
   "expect": {
    "callErrors": [ "excluded" ],
    "ledger": [
     { "code": "excluded", "scheme": "errfx.gone", "origin": "call", "delivered": true, "data": { "reason": "excluded" } }
    ],
    "hooks": { "module.callFailed": [ { "scheme": "errfx.gone", "code": "excluded", "delivered": true } ] },
    "schemeAvailable": { "errfx.gone": false }
   }
  },
